KG42.register("clusters-332ba829bb73b9797b147bc9",{"id":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v142-d-K004","paper":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences","label":"Competitive assumptions for prosumer trading participation and the platform wholesale interface","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Competitive assumptions for prosumer trading participation and the platform wholesale interface","market_meaning":"Small-scale prosumers may trade with each other within the platform and participate in wholesale trading through the platform; the platform retains the wholesale market entry point, and the platform and individual prosumers operate under price-taker assumptions at their respective stated market levels. The retailer agent is a conditional optional arrangement, and compensation when long-term competition is insufficient is retained only as a statement of possibility.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","coordination","activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Prosumers have permission to trade through the platform, which is compatible with only the platform accessing the wholesale market; price-taking behavior by the platform in the wholesale market and by prosumers within the platform belongs to different levels. The retail agent and long-term compensation respectively retain their original conditions, and the sharing of R006 only serves to reveal duplication of trading permission, not to constitute an implementation dependency.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Participating entities, tradable scope, wholesale entry, and behavioral assumptions jointly define the institutional boundary, independently of the specific allocation solution and control assignment. Optional agents and possible compensation are not expanded into already specified contractual or payment obligations.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertakes prosumer trading permission, price-taking behavior, optional retail agent, and the exception for long-term competition conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Undertakes the platform-exclusive wholesale entry and the wholesale price-taking assumption; the demand delivery clause is shared and used in v142-d-K001."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Only shares its trading permission clause to preserve the duplicated statement with R008; participants are not required to perform the control reference step first."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E10"],"rationale":"Participants' wholesale trading opportunities are realized through the platform entry; the price-taking assumptions of the two entities at different market levels are complementary, and entities or price objects are not merged on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36"],"rationale":"The small-scale prosumer trading permission within the same platform is placed respectively in the participation and execution chains; only this permission is duplicated, and the two chains as a whole are not regarded as the same rule."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M01","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E36"],"rationale":"Both procedural constraints express permission for the same entities to trade with each other through this platform and to trade into the wholesale market; the participation clause is used as the display representative, and the original execution-chain item remains accessible."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008-C004 only states that compensation may be needed when long-term competition conditions are insufficient; it does not give a definite compensation obligation, calculation method, or agent contract terms. This cluster only assembles trading permissions and behavioral assumptions and does not generate payment or fixed-price contract rules on that basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-G01-E36"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If agent contracts or incentive compensation rules need to be assembled later, source-supported trigger conditions, responsible entities, and performance methods must be supplemented separately; the current wording remains optional and possibility-oriented."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The platform's external wholesale interface is currently carried via coordination.local_operator, and there is not yet an approved independent interface object; this cannot be interpreted as all prosumers directly obtaining wholesale access.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g03-e02","v141-b-g03-e06"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-ext-wholesale-market-interface"],"required_work":"Wholesale market interface proposals and responsibility boundaries are to be handled manually; this round inserts no new nodes and modifies no existing entity or access relations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"unverified_source","description":"The basis for trading permission, platform entry, competition assumptions, and optional agents remains unreviewed B citations; assembled in this cluster does not mean these institutional descriptions have obtained independent source or scientific recognition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-G01-E36"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the permission subjects, trading paths, and conditional wording, especially preserving the non-mandatory statements of competition premises and possible compensation."}]},"rule_refs":["28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R008","28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R004","28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-28c6db1de8c06058","COMP-4f53e496ef066050","COMP-8e5c1b5bf68a422c","KG40-45833afd23977831","KG40-b1d88c1ebf1db649"]});
